{#
  The permanent address.

  §5: "/oal/v1.0 is a permanent address. It is printed on scorecards, in the changelog,
  and in the licence line. It must resolve, unchanged, indefinitely." §13 judges the
  build on whether it "renders identically in 2032, styled by 2026's stylesheet".

  So this page is self-contained: `assetBase` points its stylesheet, fonts and favicon
  at version-scoped copies taken at publication, and a colour change on the live site
  in 2028 cannot reach it. Font URLs inside styles.css are relative, so the same file
  is correct at both paths without being edited.

  Paginating over oal.versions is what makes §10's "additive by construction" true:
  publishing v1.1 adds a record to oal.json and a directory appears. What is NOT yet
  built is content immutability — see `requirePublishableVersion` in eleventy.config.js,
  which stops the build rather than let a superseded version be regenerated from a
  newer rubric.
#}
